## espeak-ng — GPL-3.0-or-later

`vendor/espeak-ng` is an unmodified submodule of https://github.com/espeak-ng/espeak-ng,
built from source by `build.rs`. Its compiled dictionary data for en, es, fr,
it, pt, and hi is embedded in this backend's binary, and the phonemizer is
linked into it. See `vendor/espeak-ng/COPYING`; parts of that project carry
Apache-2.0, BSD-2-Clause, and Unicode terms in `COPYING.APACHE`, `COPYING.BSD2`,
and `COPYING.UCD`.


## misaki — Apache-2.0

Copyright hexgrad <hello@hexgrad.com>. https://github.com/hexgrad/misaki
License: `licenses/misaki-Apache-2.0.txt`

misaki is the grapheme-to-phoneme system Kokoro was trained with, so this
backend reproduces it rather than approximating it. From misaki 0.9.4:

  * `data/en-gold-us.json.gz`, `en-gold-gb.json.gz`, `en-silver-us.json.gz`,
    and `en-silver-gb.json.gz` are its English pronunciation lexicons, copied
    verbatim and gzipped, unmodified.
  * `data/zh-ipa.tsv.gz` is derived from its Mandarin syllable-to-IPA mapping.
  * `data/ja-kana.tsv.gz`, `ja-kata-ext.tsv.gz`, and `ja-words.tsv.gz` are
    derived from `misaki.cutlet`, which is misaki's copy of cutlet
    (https://github.com/polm/cutlet, MIT, Copyright Paul O'Leary McCann).
  * `data/en-golden.tsv`, `zh-golden.tsv`, and `ja-golden.tsv` record misaki's
    own output, used as test fixtures.
  * `src/en.rs`, `src/zh.rs`, and `src/ja.rs` are ports of its algorithms,
    including the espeak rewrite table in `src/en.rs`.

`src/zh_numbers.rs` and `src/ja_numbers.rs` are original implementations that
reproduce what misaki emits for numbers — for Mandarin that is the behaviour of
cn2an (https://github.com/Ailln/cn2an, MIT), which misaki calls — rather than
ports of either. Their fixtures in `data/` are written by hand.


## pypinyin — MIT

Copyright (c) 2016 mozillazg, 闲耘 <hotoo.cn@gmail.com>
https://github.com/mozillazg/python-pinyin
License: `licenses/pypinyin-MIT.txt`

`data/zh-chars.tsv.gz` and `data/zh-phrases.tsv.gz` are built from pypinyin
0.55.0's `PINYIN_DICT` and `PHRASES_DICT`, the dictionaries misaki resolves
