## spaCy and en_core_web_sm — MIT

Copyright (C) 2016-2024 ExplosionAI GmbH, 2016 spaCy GmbH, 2015 Matthew Honnibal
https://github.com/explosion/spaCy
License: `licenses/spacy-MIT.txt`

misaki tags English with spaCy, and this backend reproduces those tags without
shipping the model:

  * `data/en-tokenizer.json.gz` is en_core_web_sm 3.8.0's tokenizer exception
    table and affix patterns, dumped verbatim.
  * `data/en-tokens.tsv` records its tokenization and tags for the fixture
    corpus, used as a test fixture.
  * `data/en-tagger.json.gz` holds averaged-perceptron weights trained on
    en_core_web_sm 3.8.0's tagger output — the model's predictions are the
    training labels, so the weights are derived from it.


## num2words — LGPL-2.1

Copyright (c) Taro Ogawa and contributors.
https://github.com/savoirfairelinux/num2words
License: `licenses/num2words-LGPL-2.1.txt`

`src/en_numbers.rs` is a Rust port of its English cardinal, ordinal, and year
verbalization, reproducing its output exactly; misaki calls num2words for the
same purpose. `data/en-numwords.tsv` records num2words' output over a numeric
sweep, and is what that port is tested against.


## Project Gutenberg — public domain

`tools/gen-en-tagger.py` trains on public-domain prose fetched from
https://www.gutenberg.org. No Gutenberg text is redistributed here — only the
tagger weights learned from it, and the texts themselves are in the public
domain in the United States.


## Fetched at runtime, not redistributed here

These are downloaded by the Super TTS daemon on the user's machine before first
use, under their own terms; no part of them is contained in this repository or
its release archives.

  * Kokoro-82M ONNX weights and voice packs, from
    https://huggingface.co/onnx-community/Kokoro-82M-v1.0-ONNX (the model is
    hexgrad/Kokoro-82M; see its model card for terms).
  * The UniDic dictionary for Japanese morphological analysis, from
    https://github.com/lindera/lindera releases.
